Still, knowledge of Google Groups Archive searching
is wonderfully useful for learning from
rec.arts.roguelike.nethack, once you have the phrase
you find interesting. The protection racket is
quite controversial, with those unskilled at it
claiming it's a death trap, which it is for them,
and those of us who do it all the time wondering
what they find difficult, so threads tend to get
very contentious, and thus hard to read, but force
yourself, there's good stuff among the dross.

This Google Groups thread starts with a nice, if far
too brief, writeup by Nigel Chapman which defines
the tactic.

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_frm/thread/5393ee2cdf84669b/1cecb9d90eb1e55f

This one in contrast starts with a "what the heck
is" sort of a posting.

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_frm/thread/26440035864d942e/14254a1f71544783

This Google Groups search misses many discussions,
because the protection racket has been called other
things here, but it will give you more than enough
material to read. Unfortunately, I type far more
than is good for me, and Google Groups searches rank
postings by how many times the phrase occurs, so a
couple of mine are at the top that aren't that
important to the topic.

http://groups.google.com/groups?q=%22the+protection+racket%22+group%3Arec.games.roguelike.nethack

The other half of the protection racket than
"arriving at the Mines Town altar at experince level
(XL) 1" is arriving there with sufficient funds. If
your luck is bad, it takes 400zx(9 offerings) to
reach the normal maximum for priest-given
protection, so where do you get 3600 zorkmids?
If your luck is good, 2400z will do.

That's where credit cloning can be a choice.

And I just happen to have written a fairly nice
tutorial on credit cloning:

http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/msg/f4db215ae79e7728

Credit cloning is even more controversial than the
protection racket -- there are people actively
lobbying to have credit cloning made impossible --
so the threads get even nastier. To see the whole
controversy, and other tutorials on credit cloning,
you can't do better than read all this:

http://groups.google.com/groups?as_epq=credit+cloning&as_ugroup=rec.games.roguelike.nethack

